  "rawFormat": "PRIMARY DATA: row-major, 2 bytes per tile in \u003CrawFile\u003E: [typeByte, collisionByte]. tiles = tilesWidth * tilesHeight. Tile (tx, ty) lives at byte index (ty * tilesWidth \u002B tx) * 2. Look up typeByte in typeByteMap and collisionByte in collisionByteMap for semantic names. collision == 0x80 means impassable; any other value means walkable. Bytes not present in typeByteMap are valid in the ROM but unclassified here \u2014 they paint magenta in the PNG (the \u0027unknown\u0027 legend color); treat as walkable by default for A* purposes and report them so a future export pass can classify them. The PNG is a derived debug visualization (one palette-encoded pixel per tile, aligned to the visible map at floor(pixel / tilePxOnVisibleMap)) \u2014 handy for diffing but lossy. Pathfinding code should consume the raw bin \u002B byte maps, not the PNG."
